	(text "The ShipFet also allows for Battery Over-current Protection.\nWith 1A current flow about a 1% is losst with this FET."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 166.624 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "139a0391-f4f8-4ca0-b0a6-d60465107150")
	)
	(text "max input current limit:\n- Solar cells will have MPPT\n- USB will detect limit with D+ and D-\n- When charging on a Powersupply the Input Current Optimizer will find the best imput current\n- The battery charging current should be limited by the REG03_Charge_Current_Limit Register\n- The back to back fets allow over 4A\n\nWe can set a limit on the REG06_Input_Current_Limit Register with a voltage on VILIM_HIZ.\nVILIM_HIZ = 1V + 800mΩ × ILIM\nI don't realy see any reson to limit the input current.\nThe Datasheet gives a maximum of 3.3A input current so let's leave some margin and go for 3A.\n1V + 800mΩ * 3A = 3.4V\nVoltage devider from REGN = 5V\n680k*(5V/3.4V - 1) = 320k\n\nThe ILIM_HIZ-Pin might leak +- 1.5uA\n(Connect ILIM_HIZ to REGN to set the maximum input current limit.)\n( could this pin be used to put the IC in High Impedance mode? )"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.764 164.846 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2aaaf896-0a57-4919-bda9-bf1e122b4810")
	)
	(text "BQ25798\nMPPT\nEfficiency for conversion to 1s Battery Charge better 90%\nBATFET 11mR\nBattery Lade/Entlade effizienz?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.526 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "77d58056-c61b-4015-a8c8-c464951ca6b2")
	)
	(text "10V, 4.7μF "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.674 81.026 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
